### Org Verification Module - HTTP Test Collection

# Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@contentType = application/json

# Store session cookies for authenticated requests
@sessionCookie =

---

### 1. Register a new user (setup for signup)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-up
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "hospital-admin@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!",
  "name": "Hospital Admin"
}

> {%
  // Store the session from response headers
  client.global.set('sessionCookie', response.headers.valueOfHeader('set-cookie'));
%}

---

### 2. Sign up a new hospital organization
POST {{baseUrl}}/organizations/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "name": "Central Medical Hospital",
  "slug": "central-medical-hospital",
  "type": "hospital",
  "address": "123 Medical Lane, Healthcare City, HC 12345",
  "licenseDocUrl": "https://example.com/licenses/central-medical-hospital-license.pdf",
  "metadata": "Founded in 1995, serves 50,000+ patients annually"
}

> {%
  // Store the organization ID for later requests
  if (response.status === 201) {
    const data = response.body;
    client.global.set('organizationId', data.organization.id);
  }
%}

---

### 3. Register a super_admin user (for review operations)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-up
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "super-admin@example.com",
  "password": "AdminPassword123!",
  "name": "Super Admin"
}

> {%
  // Store the super admin session
  client.global.set('superAdminSessionCookie', response.headers.valueOfHeader('set-cookie'));
%}

---

### 4. Grant super_admin role to the admin user
# Note: This would typically be done via a seeds script or internal admin API
# For now, you'll need to manually set the role in the database or via an admin endpoint
# UPDATE "auth"."user" SET role = 'super_admin' WHERE email = 'super-admin@example.com';

---

### 5. List pending organizations (super_admin only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/organizations/pending
Cookie: {{superAdminSessionCookie}}

---

### 6. Approve a hospital organization
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/organizations/{{organizationId}}/review
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Cookie: {{superAdminSessionCookie}}

{
  "decision": "approved",
  "reason": "Documentation verified, facility meets all requirements"
}

---

### 7. Get organization verification status (as organization member)
GET {{baseUrl}}/organizations/{{organizationId}}/status
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

---

### 8. Sign up a second hospital (for testing flagged state)
POST {{baseUrl}}/organizations/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "name": "Secondary Health Center",
  "slug": "secondary-health-center",
  "type": "hospital",
  "address": "456 Care Avenue, Wellness District, WD 67890",
  "licenseDocUrl": "https://example.com/licenses/secondary-health-center-license.pdf"
}

> {%
  // Store the second organization ID
  if (response.status === 201) {
    const data = response.body;
    client.global.set('organizationId2', data.organization.id);
  }
%}

---

### 9. Flag a hospital organization
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/organizations/{{organizationId2}}/review
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Cookie: {{superAdminSessionCookie}}

{
  "decision": "flagged",
  "reason": "License documentation incomplete, requires resubmission"
}

---

### 10. Try to approve an already-approved organization (idempotency test)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/organizations/{{organizationId}}/review
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Cookie: {{superAdminSessionCookie}}

{
  "decision": "approved",
  "reason": "Duplicate approval attempt"
}

# Expected: 409 Conflict - "Organization is already approved. Cannot re-process."

---

### 11. Get status of flagged organization (as member)
GET {{baseUrl}}/organizations/{{organizationId2}}/status
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

---

### 12. Test invalid input - missing required field
POST {{baseUrl}}/organizations/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "name": "Incomplete Hospital",
  "slug": "incomplete-hospital"
  # Missing: type, address, licenseDocUrl
}

# Expected: 400 Bad Request - validation error

---

### 13. Test invalid input - invalid type
POST {{baseUrl}}/organizations/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "name": "Invalid Type Hospital",
  "slug": "invalid-type-hospital",
  "type": "invalid_type",
  "address": "123 Main St",
  "licenseDocUrl": "https://example.com/license.pdf"
}

# Expected: 400 Bad Request - "type must be one of: hospital, campaign_organizer"

---

### 14. Test invalid input - invalid URL
POST {{baseUrl}}/organizations/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "name": "Invalid URL Hospital",
  "slug": "invalid-url-hospital",
  "type": "hospital",
  "address": "123 Main St",
  "licenseDocUrl": "not-a-valid-url"
}

# Expected: 400 Bad Request - "licenseDocUrl must be a URL"

---

### 15. Test duplicate slug conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/organizations/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "name": "Different Hospital Name",
  "slug": "central-medical-hospital",
  "type": "hospital",
  "address": "789 Different St",
  "licenseDocUrl": "https://example.com/license2.pdf"
}

# Expected: 409 Conflict - "Organization slug 'central-medical-hospital' already exists"

---

### 16. Test unauthorized access - list pending without super_admin role
GET {{baseUrl}}/organizations/pending
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

# Expected: 403 Forbidden - User must have super_admin role

---

### 17. Test unauthorized access - review without super_admin role
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/organizations/{{organizationId}}/review
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "decision": "approved"
}

# Expected: 403 Forbidden - User must have super_admin role

---

### 18. Test access to status endpoint as non-member
# First, create another user account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-up
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "unrelated-user@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "name": "Unrelated User"
}

> {%
  client.global.set('unrelatedUserCookie', response.headers.valueOfHeader('set-cookie'));
%}

---

### 19. Attempt status check as non-member (should be forbidden)
GET {{baseUrl}}/organizations/{{organizationId}}/status
Cookie: {{unrelatedUserCookie}}

# Expected: 403 Forbidden - User must be a member of this organization

---

### 20. Test campaign_organizer type signup
POST {{baseUrl}}/organizations/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "name": "Red Cross Blood Drive 2026",
  "slug": "red-cross-blood-drive-2026",
  "type": "campaign_organizer",
  "address": "321 Community Center, Blood Drive City, BD 54321",
  "licenseDocUrl": "https://example.com/licenses/red-cross-registration.pdf"
}

---

### Test Flow Summary

# Workflow for manual testing:
# 1. Create hospital-admin user (request #1) - get sessionCookie
# 2. Sign up hospital organization (request #2) - get organizationId
# 3. Create super-admin user (request #3) - get superAdminSessionCookie
# 4. Manually grant super_admin role in database
# 5. List pending (request #5)
# 6. Approve organization (request #6)
# 7. Get status as member (request #7)
# 8. Sign up second hospital (request #8) - get organizationId2
# 9. Flag second organization (request #9)
# 10. Test idempotency (request #10)
# 11. Test validation errors (requests #12-15)
# 12. Test authorization (requests #16-17)
# 13. Test campaign organizer type (request #20)

---

### Notes

# For Thunder Client users:
# 1. Import this file as a REST API collection
# 2. The @ variables will be stored in collection-level environment variables
# 3. Use the > blocks to execute tests and set variables

# For Postman users:
# Convert this to Postman collection format (JSON) and import
# Postman script examples provided below for reference

# For curl users:
# Extract individual requests and convert to curl format as needed

# Database setup for testing:
# 1. Ensure migrations are applied: npx prisma migrate deploy
# 2. Optional: Seed database with test data using prisma/seed.ts
# 3. For super_admin role, manually update:
#    UPDATE "auth"."user" SET role = 'super_admin' WHERE email = 'super-admin@example.com';
